-- statement:
--   The definitions of the module `MIPRE.Background.QLD.RegisterForm` of the MIP\* = RE formalization (commit `70cbf1c` of vidick/MIPRE-formalization). `thm:qld` in the register-first form its consumer reads. The swap isometry lemma (`MirrorSimul.swap_isometry`) concludes on the *physical* registers: each party holds `H × Anc`, its half of the maximally entangled pair **last**, and the product state is `outerUnVec (auxVec aux)`, with value `aux (x, y) * epr (a, b)` at `((x, a), (y, b))`. Its consumer, the introspection soundness theorem (`TypedEstimates.quantumValue_ge_of_valid_isometric_images`), reads the same objects with the register **first**: isometries `VA : Matrix ((ι → F) × H) H₀ ℂ`, the state `registerState (ι → F) ξ`, with value…
--
--   **Definitions** (2): `MIPRE.QLD.regFirst` (**Put the register first.** An isometry into `H × T`, read as one into `T × H`: the same matrix with its row labels swapped.); `MIPRE.QLD.regSwap` (The relabelling of both parties at once, as an equivalence.).
